WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:05.760
Just weeks after announcing his triumphant&nbsp;
return as Superman, Henry Cavill had to take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:10.440
it all back. Here's how some DC diehards&nbsp;
are fighting the studio's decision.
 &nbsp;

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:15.480
When the news first dropped that director&nbsp;
James Gunn and producer Peter Safran would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:21.000
take charge of the DC film universe, under&nbsp;
new Warner Bros. Discovery CEO David Zaslav,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:25.200
it was implied that the duo would attempt to steer&nbsp;
the franchise in something of a new direction.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:31.680
In one surprising move under their stewardship,&nbsp;
longtime DC Superman actor Henry Cavill revealed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:36.600
that he's Superman no longer — though a&nbsp;
new "Superman" movie is planned, and Gunn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:41.340
intends to maintain a working relationship with&nbsp;
Cavill moving forward. Gunn posted on Twitter,

00:00:57.153 --> 00:00:58.860
On Instagram, Cavill shared,

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:19.440
Now that Cavill is a free agent, fans of&nbsp;
other major movie franchises have begun&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:24.360
to propose ideas for his next big role. For&nbsp;
instance, some want Cavill to join the MCU,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:29.280
given his superhero experience and,&nbsp;
presumably, his superhero movie-ready physique.

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:34.320
Meanwhile, others think Cavill is a good fit for&nbsp;
James Bond, especially with the role's current&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:39.780
vacancy in mind. Of course, Cavill may instead&nbsp;
separate himself from franchise films entirely,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:44.160
with his "Superman" exit following his&nbsp;
departure from Netflix's "The Witcher."

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:49.260
"Enjoy your last walk across the&nbsp;
meadow, and through the mist."

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:54.600
Whatever his future may be, plenty of fans&nbsp;
are, unsurprisingly, unhappy about Cavill's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:58.680
departure. In fact, some are going so far as&nbsp;
to call for Gunn's head over the decision.

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:02.760
Soon after Henry Cavill's departure&nbsp;
from the DC film universe broke,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:06.240
users on Twitter began to share&nbsp;
their disappointment with James Gunn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:10.380
specifically over the news under&nbsp;
the hashtag #FireJamesGunn.

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:15.000
One user shared a screenshot of Cavill's&nbsp;
Instagram post confirming his departure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:21.060
with the caption "#FireJamesGunn pass it on."&nbsp;
Meanwhile, in another post utilizing the hashtag,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:25.440
another user argued that this news is&nbsp;
particularly disappointing given both&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:30.360
Cavill's apparent interest in remaining Superman,&nbsp;
and the fact that "Black Adam" seemed to tease a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:34.690
future Cavill Superman storyline upon its&nbsp;
release about a month and a half prior.

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:38.830
"Black Adam. We should talk."

00:02:38.830 --> 00:02:42.960
The hashtag has generated plenty of&nbsp;
discussion beyond just these posts too,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:46.860
to the extent that the conversation has&nbsp;
reached at least one additional platform.

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:51.960
Eventually, discussion of James Gunn's firing&nbsp;
over his decision to proceed without Henry Cavill&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:56.580
reached enough of a critical mass that someone&nbsp;
started a Change.org petition for the cause.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.580 --> 00:03:02.400
This petition names Warner Bros. Discovery&nbsp;
CEO David Zaslav as its intended audience,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:07.620
urging him to rehire Cavill and fire&nbsp;
Gunn, arguing that Cavill is a bonafide&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:12.720
movie star and capable of generating more&nbsp;
revenue than Gunn can as one of DC's leads.

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:18.960
As of the making of this video, the petition has&nbsp;
garnered 500 signatures and climbing. While such&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:24.180
a petition is unlikely to influence Zaslav or&nbsp;
affect Cavill's career, the amount of signatures&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:28.560
it ultimately receives can nevertheless serve&nbsp;
as a measure of the degree to which those upset&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:32.700
about Cavill's firing think that Gunn's&nbsp;
job should be impacted by this decision.

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:37.740
Of course, these sentiments aren't reflective of&nbsp;
DC film fans as a whole, but are, nevertheless,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:42.300
in steady circulation following&nbsp;
the Cavill news. Gunn and Peter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:47.100
Safran are still at the start of their DC&nbsp;
journey, so once the DC film universe has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:50.950
time to develop under their guidance,&nbsp;
such sentiments could very well change.

